```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 <style>
 body {
 font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
 margin: 0;
 padding: 20px;
 }
 .responsive-table {
 width: 100%;
 border-collapse: collapse;
 margin-top: 20px;
 }
 .responsive-table th, .responsive-table td {
 border: 1px solid #ddd;
 padding: 8px;
 text-align: left;
 }
 .responsive-table th {
 background-color: #f4f4f4;
 }
 .responsive-table tr:nth-child(even) {
 background-color: #f9f9f9;
 }
 .responsive-table tr:hover {
 background-color: #e0e0e0;
 }
 @media screen and (max-width: 600px) {
 .responsive-table {
 border: 0;
 }
 .responsive-table thead {
 display: none;
 }
 .responsive-table tr {
 display: block;
 margin-bottom: 10px;
 }
 .responsive-table td {
 display: block;
 text-align: right;
 padding-left: 50%;
 position: relative;
 }
 .responsive-table td::before {
 content: attr(data-label);
 position: absolute;
 left: 0;
 width: 50%;
 padding-left: 15px;
 font-weight: bold;
 text-align: left;
 }
 }
 </style>
</head>
<body>
 <h2>Responsive Table Example</h2>
 <table class="responsive-table">
 <thead>
 <tr>
 <th>Name</th>
 <th>Age</th>
 <th>Occupation</th>
 </tr>
 </thead>
 <tbody>
 <tr>
 <td data-label="Name">Alice Johnson</td>
 <td data-label="Age">29</td>
 <td data-label="Occupation">Engineer</td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
 <td data-label="Name">Bob Smith</td>
 <td data-label="Age">34</td>
 <td data-label="Occupation">Designer</td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
 <td data-label="Name">Carlos Diaz</td>
 <td data-label="Age">41</td>
 <td data-label="Occupation">Developer</td>
 </tr>
 </tbody>
 </table>
</body>
</html>
```

This example uses media queries to adapt the table for smaller screens, ensuring each row stacks vertically. The `::before` pseudo-element helps add a label to each cell, improving readability on mobile devices.

