### HTML and CSS for Contact Form:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 <title>Contact Form</title>
 <style>
 .contact-form {
 width: 300px;
 margin: 0 auto;
 padding: 20px;
 border: 1px solid #ccc;
 border-radius: 5px;
 box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
 }
 .contact-form h2 {
 text-align: center;
 margin-bottom: 1em;
 }
 .form-control {
 margin-bottom: 1em;
 }
 .form-control label {
 display: block;
 margin-bottom: 0.3em;
 }
 .form-control input {
 width: 100%;
 padding: 0.5em;
 border: 1px solid #ccc;
 border-radius: 4px;
 }
 .form-control input:invalid {
 border-color: #e74c3c;
 }
 .form-control input:valid {
 border-color: #2ecc71;
 }
 .submit-btn {
 width: 100%;
 padding: 0.5em;
 background-color: #3498db;
 color: #fff;
 border: none;
 border-radius: 4px;
 cursor: pointer;
 }
 .error-message {
 color: #e74c3c;
 font-size: 0.9em;
 }
 </style>
</head>
<body>
 <div class="contact-form">
 <h2>Contact Us</h2>
 <form id="contactForm">
 <div class="form-control">
 <label for="name">Name</label>
 <input type="text" id="name" name="name" required minlength="2">
 <span class="error-message" id="nameError">Please enter your name.</span>
 </div>
 <div class="form-control">
 <label for="email">Email</label>
 <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required>
 <span class="error-message" id="emailError">Please provide a valid email address.</span>
 </div>
 <div class="form-control">
 <label for="message">Message</label>
 <textarea id="message" name="message" required minlength="10"></textarea>
 <span class="error-message" id="messageError">Your message should be at least 10 characters long.</span>
 </div>
 <button type="submit" class="submit-btn">Send Message</button>
 </form>
 </div>

 <script>
 const contactForm = document.getElementById('contactForm');

 contactForm.addEventListener('submit', function(event) {
 const name = document.getElementById('name');
 const email = document.getElementById('email');
 const message = document.getElementById('message');

 if (!name.checkValidity()) {
 document.getElementById('nameError').style.display = 'inline';
 event.preventDefault();
 }

 if (!email.checkValidity()) {
 document.getElementById('emailError').style.display = 'inline';
 event.preventDefault();
 }

 if (!message.checkValidity()) {
 document.getElementById('messageError').style.display = 'inline';
 event.preventDefault();
 }
 });
 </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
- **HTML Structure**: It includes fields for name, email, and message, each with associated error messages that appear when validation fails.
- **CSS Styling**: Adds basic styles, ensuring the form is neat and styled consistently with red borders for invalid inputs and green for valid ones.
- **JavaScript**: Implements client-side validation by listening for the form's submit event and checking each field's validity. Displays error messages if any field is invalid.

