 .hidden {
 display: none;
 }
 .form-control {
 margin: 1em 0;
 }
 </style>
</head>
<body>
 <form id="dynamic-form">
 <div class="form-control">
 <label for="account-type">Account Type:</label>
 <select id="account-type" name="account-type">
 <option value="">Select...</option>
 <option value="personal">Personal</option>
 <option value="business">Business</option>
 </select>
 </div>

 <div class="form-control hidden" id="business-name">
 <label for="business-name">Business Name:</label>
 <input type="text" id="business-name-input" name="business-name">
 </div>

 <div class="form-control hidden" id="additional-info">
 <label for="additional-info">Additional Info:</label>
 <textarea id="additional-info-text" name="additional-info"></textarea>
 </div>

 <button type="submit">Submit</button>
 </form>

 <script>
 const accountTypeSelect = document.getElementById('account-type');
 const businessNameField = document.getElementById('business-name');
 const additionalInfoField = document.getElementById('additional-info');

 accountTypeSelect.addEventListener('change', function() {
 const value = this.value;
 if (value === 'business') {
 businessNameField.classList.remove('hidden');
 additionalInfoField.classList.add('hidden');
 } else if (value === 'personal') {
 additionalInfoField.classList.remove('hidden');
 businessNameField.classList.add('hidden');
 } else {
 businessNameField.classList.add('hidden');
 additionalInfoField.classList.add('hidden');
 }
 });
 </script>
</body>
</html>
```

**Explanation:**
- **HTML Structure:** The form contains a dropdown for selecting the account type. Depending on the selection, different fields are shown or hidden.
- **CSS:** The `.hidden` class is used to control the visibility of the fields.
- **JavaScript:** An event listener on the dropdown monitors changes and toggles field visibility based on the selection.

This is a basic example, but it showcases the core concept of dynamic form fields based on user input. You can expand this logic to include more complex dependencies as needed.

