```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 <title>Responsive Navigation Menu</title>
 <style>
 body {
 font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
 margin: 0;
 padding: 0;
 }
 .nav-header {
 background-color: #333;
 color: #fff;
 padding: 10px 20px;
 display: flex;
 justify-content: space-between;
 align-items: center;
 }
 .nav-title {
 font-size: 1.5em;
 margin: 0;
 }
 .nav-toggle {
 background-color: #444;
 border: none;
 color: white;
 padding: 10px;
 cursor: pointer;
 display: none;
 }
 nav {
 display: flex;
 justify-content: space-around;
 background-color: #444;
 }
 nav a {
 color: white;
 padding: 14px 20px;
 text-decoration: none;
 }
 nav a:hover {
 background-color: #555;
 }
 @media (max-width: 600px) {
 .nav-toggle {
 display: block;
 }
 nav {
 display: none;
 flex-direction: column;
 width: 100%;
 }
 nav.active {
 display: flex;
 }
 }
 </style>
</head>
<body>
 <header class="nav-header">
 <h1 class="nav-title">Website</h1>
 <button class="nav-toggle" aria-label="Toggle navigation menu" aria-expanded="false">
 ☰ Menu
 </button>
 </header>
 <nav>
 <a href="#">Home</a>
 <a href="#">About</a>
 <a href="#">Services</a>
 <a href="#">Contact</a>
 </nav>
 <script>
 const toggleButton = document.querySelector('.nav-toggle');
 const nav = document.querySelector('nav');

 toggleButton.addEventListener('click', () => {
 const expanded = toggleButton.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true' || false;
 toggleButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded', !expanded);
 nav.classList.toggle('active');
 });
 </script>
</body>
</html>
```

**How it works:**
- **Responsive Design:** The menu collapses into a toggle button on screens smaller than 600px.
- **Accessibility:** The toggle button uses `aria-label` and `aria-expanded` attributes to convey its status to screen readers.
- **Styling:** The CSS ensures a clean, modern look across devices.

I hope this helps you create an accessible and responsive navigation menu!

