 <style>
 body {
 font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
 margin: 0;
 padding: 0;
 }
 .nav-bar {
 background-color: #333;
 overflow: hidden;
 }
 .menu {
 display: none;
 flex-direction: column;
 position: absolute;
 background-color: #333;
 width: 100%;
 top: 50px;
 }
 .menu a {
 padding: 16px;
 text-decoration: none;
 color: white;
 text-align: center;
 }
 .menu a:hover {
 background-color: #575757;
 }
 .toggle-btn {
 font-size: 18px;
 padding: 15px;
 color: white;
 cursor: pointer;
 background-color: #333;
 border: none;
 width: 100%;
 text-align: left;
 }
 @media (min-width: 600px) {
 .menu {
 display: flex;
 position: static;
 flex-direction: row;
 }
 .toggle-btn {
 display: none;
 }
 }
 </style>
</head>
<body>
 <nav class="nav-bar">
 <button class="toggle-btn" onclick="toggleMenu()">&#9776; Menu</button>
 <div class="menu" id="navMenu">
 <a href="#home">Home</a>
 <a href="#services">Services</a>
 <a href="#about">About</a>
 <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
 </div>
 </nav>
 <script>
 function toggleMenu() {
 var menu = document.getElementById('navMenu');
 if (menu.style.display === 'block') {
 menu.style.display = 'none';
 } else {
 menu.style.display = 'block';
 }
 }
 </script>
</body>
</html>
```

**Explanation:**
- The **nav-bar** is the container for your navigation.
- The **menu** is initially hidden and displayed in a column layout on smaller screens.
- The **toggle-btn** is used to show or hide the menu on click, and it disappears on larger screens where the menu is always shown.
- The JavaScript function `toggleMenu()` toggles the display property of the menu for interactivity.

This code ensures that your navigation is responsive and works seamlessly across different devices and browsers. Feel free to customize the colors and styles as needed!

