<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 <title>Responsive Navigation Header</title>
 <style>
 body {
 margin: 0;
 font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
 }
 .header {
 display: flex;
 justify-content: space-between;
 align-items: center;
 padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
 background-color: #333;
 color: white;
 }
 .header .logo {
 font-size: 1.5rem;
 font-weight: bold;
 }
 .nav-menu {
 display: flex;
 list-style: none;
 padding: 0;
 }
 .nav-menu li {
 margin-left: 1rem;
 }
 .nav-menu a {
 text-decoration: none;
 color: white;
 transition: color 0.3s ease;
 }
 .nav-menu a:hover {
 color: #ff6347;
 }
 @media (max-width: 768px) {
 .nav-menu {
 display: none;
 flex-direction: column;
 position: absolute;
 top: 100%;
 left: 0;
 right: 0;
 background-color: #333;
 padding: 1rem;
 }
 .header {
 flex-direction: column;
 align-items: flex-start;
 }
 .menu-toggle {
 display: block;
 cursor: pointer;
 margin-left: auto;
 }
 }
 </style>
</head>
<body>
 <header class="header">
 <div class="logo">MySite</div>
 <span class="menu-toggle">☰</span>
 <ul class="nav-menu">
 <li><a href="#">Home</a></li>
 <li><a href="#">About</a></li>
 <li><a href="#">Services</a></li>
 <li><a href="#">Contact</a></li>
 </ul>
 </header>

 <script>
 const toggle = document.querySelector('.menu-toggle');
 const menu = document.querySelector('.nav-menu');

 toggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
 menu.style.display = menu.style.display === 'block' ? 'none' : 'block';
 });
 </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Key Features:
- **Flexbox** is used for layout alignment, ensuring the header adjusts neatly across different screen sizes.
- **Media Queries** hide the navigation links on smaller screens, displaying them only when the toggle button is clicked.
- **JavaScript** enables toggling of the navigation menu on smaller screens, enhancing mobile usability.

