```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 <style>
 body {
 font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
 }
 .sidebar {
 width: 250px;
 background-color: #f4f4f4;
 padding: 15px;
 border-right: 1px solid #ddd;
 }
 .accordion {
 background-color: #eee;
 color: #444;
 cursor: pointer;
 padding: 10px;
 width: 100%;
 border: none;
 text-align: left;
 outline: none;
 transition: 0.4s;
 margin-bottom: 10px;
 }
 .active, .accordion:hover {
 background-color: #ccc;
 }
 .panel {
 padding: 0 10px;
 display: none;
 background-color: white;
 overflow: hidden;
 }
 </style>
 <title>Accordion Menu</title>
</head>
<body>

<div class="sidebar">
 <button class="accordion">Section 1</button>
 <div class="panel">
 <p>This is the content of Section 1.</p>
 </div>
 <button class="accordion">Section 2</button>
 <div class="panel">
 <p>This is the content of Section 2.</p>
 </div>
 <button class="accordion">Section 3</button>
 <div class="panel">
 <p>This is the content of Section 3.</p>
 </div>
</div>

<script>
 var acc = document.getElementsByClassName("accordion");
 var i;

 for (i = 0; i < acc.length; i++) {
 acc[i].addEventListener("click", function() {
 this.classList.toggle("active");
 var panel = this.nextElementSibling;
 if (panel.style.display === "block") {
 panel.style.display = "none";
 } else {
 panel.style.display = "block";
 }
 });
 }
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

**Explanation:**
- **HTML Structure:** The sidebar contains a series of buttons with the class "accordion" and corresponding "panel" divs that hold the content for each section.
- **CSS Styling:** Basic styles are applied for a clean and minimal look, with transitions for smooth opening and closing effects.
- **JavaScript Functionality:** A simple script toggles the display of panels when the accordion buttons are clicked.

