```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 <title>Responsive Collapsible Menu</title>
 <style>
 body {
 font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
 margin: 0;
 padding: 0;
 }
 .header {
 background-color: #4CAF50;
 overflow: hidden;
 }
 .nav-links {
 display: none;
 flex-direction: column;
 background-color: #333;
 width: 100%;
 }
 .nav-links a {
 padding: 14px 20px;
 text-decoration: none;
 color: white;
 text-align: center;
 }
 .nav-links a:hover {
 background-color: #575757;
 }
 .toggle-button {
 background-color: #4CAF50;
 border: none;
 color: white;
 padding: 14px 20px;
 cursor: pointer;
 width: 100%;
 }
 @media(min-width: 600px) {
 .nav-links {
 display: flex;
 flex-direction: row;
 justify-content: space-around;
 }
 .toggle-button {
 display: none;
 }
 }
 </style>
 <script>
 function toggleMenu() {
 const navLinks = document.querySelector('.nav-links');
 if (navLinks.style.display === "flex") {
 navLinks.style.display = "none";
 } else {
 navLinks.style.display = "flex";
 }
 }
 </script>
</head>
<body>
 <header class="header">
 <button class="toggle-button" onclick="toggleMenu()">☰ Menu</button>
 <nav class="nav-links">
 <a href="#home">Home</a>
 <a href="#about">About</a>
 <a href="#services">Services</a>
 <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
 </nav>
 </header>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
- **Header**: Contains a button for toggling and a navigation menu.
- **Toggle Button**: When clicked, it calls the `toggleMenu()` JavaScript function to show or hide the navigation links.
- **Media Query**: The CSS media query ensures that the menu becomes a horizontal list on screens wider than 600px, and the toggle button is hidden.

